|term[universal-path] :status settled :defined-by def-locations-and-paths :anchor universal-location
  :word universal-path
  :synonyms [absolute-path]
  :avoid [universal-location]
  A [[term/path]] routable to its destination from any origin (within a bounded context).
  |invariants
    - Is a kind of [[term/path]]
    - Is a path whose [[term/origin]] manner is universal ([[DECISIONS#d11-universal-path|D11 universal-path]])
    - Is the exact condition under which path, location, and identity safely interchange — the "Universal" URI/URN/URL presuppose
